WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.780
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for Game of Thrones I wanted to do a Direwolf

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.780
video.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.280
Because the show is playing it a little fast
and loose with the books I’ll do a quick

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.070
recap of where they all are dead or alive
as we head into season 5.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:20.199
I’m going to spend more time on the ones
that are still alive.

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:23.810
For the most part the show has caught up with
the Direwolves book story.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.420
Speaking of which, I’m giving away another
copy of World of Ice and Fire all you have

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.769
to do to enter is be a subscriber and leave
a comment on this video.

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:33.930
At a certain point I will talk about some
Winds of Winter Direwolf theories that George

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:43.960
RR Martin has confirmed publicly so just general
Spoiler Warning for everything through season

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:44.960
4 on the show and the direwolves in the books.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:45.960
I’m going to skip talking about the characters
so don’t worry about spoilers for them.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.450
Starting off, where are they?

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:53.120
Grey Wind was murdered with Robb Stark during
the Red Wedding, Lady was killed by Ned Stark

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.850
during their journey to King’s Landing,
even though Sophie Turner adopted her direwolf

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:57.850
in real life.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.170
Best way for an animal actor to leave a show.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.809
Viggo Mortensen did the same thing with his
horse from Lord of the Rings after they finished

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:05.809
the last film.

00:01:05.809 --> 00:01:10.280
Nymeria was turned loose by Arya and is still
alive, presumed running around in the Riverlands.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.619
A lot of this video will be devoted to her.

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:19.630
Summer is chilling out with Bran and the Bloodraven
underneath the giant weirwood north of the

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.630
wall.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:21.630
Shaggydog is in hiding with Rickon and Osha.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.630
I’ll explain more about what’s going on
with them since they dropped off the map on

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:23.630
the show and in the books.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.010
and Ghost is at Castle Black with Jon Snow

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.381
Up to this point the show hasn’t changed
anything major about each of the direwolves

00:01:28.381 --> 00:01:29.381
from the books.

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:31.810
They’ve just omitted stuff or brushed over
it lightly.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.409
So 4 of the original 6 are still alive and
no, I don’t think we’ll see any of them

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:36.619
reanimated by white walkers.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:42.140
I always get a lot of questions about dead
characters people want to see turned into

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.500
wights.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.280
One of my favorite things about the direwolves
are that they are bonded to the Stark children

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.060
just like Dragons bonded with the Valyrians
or Daenerys’ dragons bonded with her, to

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.500
go with a more current reference.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.090
I’d go so far as to say that the relationship
between the Starks and their direwolves is

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:08.789
even closer because of their ability 
to warg.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:17.520
I think George RR Martin hasn’t officially
said whether or not all the Stark children

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.570
are able to warg but it’s implied.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.200
Bran is the only one so far that has actually
explored that ability.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.330
But he’s extra special because he’s also
a greenseer.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.910
Which is super rare even amongst wargs.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.110
Any time they have dreams of running around
it’s a low level passive warg.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:39.260
I think if all the direwolves were still alive
Sansa and Robb would have the dreams too.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.460
The show hasn’t given us Jon or Rickon dreams
but that’s only because they’re non-essential

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.540
to the stories they’ve told so far.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:53.380
I’ve already done a video about some of
the biggest things the show is NOT doing in

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.380
season 5.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.460
I think people are slowly getting used to
that.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:04.710
Because of all the things they’ve cut out
I don’t think we’ll see Nymeria, Summer

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.460
or Shaggydog anytime soon.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:11.290
Dave and Dan confirmed we’d open season
5 with a flashback but that Bran’s group

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.700
had already passed their book story so the
actors are in a holding pattern until the

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.300
rest of the show catches up.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:23.503
Just to clarify, Arya at the end of season
4 is right at the beginning of her story in

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.503
Book 4.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:32.120
But Bran is at the end of his story in book
5.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:39.600
So there’s no more story to tell for Bran
until George RR Martin finishes Winds of Winter.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.160
Unless Dan and Dave make up their own story,
which I don’t think any of us want.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.160
So some people on the show are further ahead
of their book story than others.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.160
It sounds weird I know.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.530
The problem with not including extra small
things is that Nymeria is one of the most

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:53.750
interesting direwolves, Ghost is awesome,
but Nymeria is on a very similar arc to Arya

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.750
Stark.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.750
Similar but not the same.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.040
I’m going to be talking about book stuff
here so I’ll put this spoiler tag up.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.620
Things that George RR Martin says in open
public forum aren’t really spoilers but

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.620
just in case.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.290
Nymeria is still alive running around the
Riverlands.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:15.130
The last time she was referenced she had created
a growing pack of normal wolves.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:18.820
She’s the size of a pony so she’s always
going to be the Alpha.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.990
By the end of book 5 it’s implied that they’ve
become a super pack.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:29.060
Normal wolf packs in real life can get as
big as 15.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:36.880
George RR Martin confirmed that the Nymeria
superpack would play an important role in

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:37.880
the future.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.330
He didn’t say how but he made a very chekov’s
gun type of joke.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.510
For anyone who’s not a theater geek that
just means that an author will never put a

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.750
weapon in a story without intending it to
be used.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:48.880
Nymeria’s pack is that weapon.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.250
Although there isn’t a human character pulling
the trigger.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.680
I said all the Starks who’s direwolves are
still alive have warg dreams.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.520
Arya still has them regardless of where she
travels in the world.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:58.970
Just to avoid crazy season 5 spoilers.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.140
Even though I don’t think season 5 will
do any Nymeria scenes here’s what I think

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.430
will happen with the super pack in Winds of
Winter.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:07.090
There’s all this tension building as Stannis
marches his army to Winterfell to fight the

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.290
Boltons and the Freys.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.230
Who are largely fighting amongst themselves
anyway.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:18.500
I’d really like to see the superpack engage
the battle when Stannis actually meets the

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.500
Bolton/Frey army.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.820
It would be sweet revenge for the Red Wedding.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:27.080
The riverlands which is where it’s assumed
they still are is really far south, but wolves

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.390
run so fast that it doesn’t seem ridiculous
that they could get involved.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.850
Of all the battles teased in book 5, the battle
of Winterfell is the biggest.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.710
I just feel like that would be the biggest
payoff.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.010
Okay, so spoilers over.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.960
Here’s my question for you guys.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:46.850
What do you want to see happen with the direwolves
in season 5 or in the books?

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:52.310
Just remember, as winter and white walkers
slowly descend on the south and food becomes

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:55.910
more scarce.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:06:05.920
Meat is meat and direwolves have 
to eat.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.930
I know I referenced some winds of winter predictions,
there’s still no official release date although

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.670
I’d put it sometime in 2016 at this point.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:16.480
Finger crossed it’s by spring or summer.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.490
I don’t want to have to wait till november
2016.

